21-v3","violation_type_id":"tx-tac-746-801-5","inspection_id":"tx-hhsc-1064609-i20260521","date":"2026-05-21","original_code":"746.801(5)","severity":"medium","severity_label":"Medium risk","status":"corrected","status_label":"Correction verified 2026-06-08","finding":"Required Records Maintained and Made Available - Employees' Attendance: There were no time sheets available for review for both directors.","topic":"supervision","source_record_id":"1026542814","violation_type_title":"Required Records Maintained and Made Available - Employees' Attendance (26 TAC §746.801(5))","topic_label":"Supervision & ratios"},{"id":"tx-hhsc-1064609-i20260521-v4","violation_type_id":"tx-tac-746-3317-8","inspection_id":"tx-hhsc-1064609-i20260521","date":"2026-05-21","original_code":"746.3317(8)","severity":"medium_high","severity_label":"Medium-high risk","status":"corrected","status_label":"Correction verified 2026-06-08","finding":"Food Service and Preparation Requirement - Cover All Stored Food: A bowl with fruit was observed uncovered in the refrigerator.    Note: This was addressed during inspection and the fruit was removed from the bowl and stored in a sealed plastic bag.","topic":"supervision","source_record_id":"1026261717","violation_type_title":"Food Service and Preparation Requirement - Cover All Stored Food (26 TAC §746.3317(8))","topic_label":"Supervision & ratios"},{"id":"tx-hhsc-1064609-i20260521-v5","violation_type_id":"tx-tac-746-1605-1","inspection_id":"tx-hhsc-1064609-i20260521","date":"2026-05-21","original_code":"746.1605(1)","severity":"medium_high","severity_label":"Medium-high risk","status":"corrected","status_label":"Correction verified 2026-06-08","finding":"Child/Caregiver Ratio - 18 Months Difference in Age: Two caregivers were caring for 7 children of varying ages including infants in a toddler room during the naptime. The children combined were five toddler children and two infants. There was more than 18 month difference between the youngest child an